  "decision_status": "READY_TO_EXECUTE",
  "scientific_rationale": "PROP-003 conducts a formal interaction test between commute_5h and sex for the sleep outcome, directly addressing the untested hypothesis H3 left by EXP-001. It has the highest expected information gain (HIGH) and can discriminate whether the observed strongest negative point estimate for sleep varies by sex, which could explain the inconclusive ranking of personal‑time dimensions. The engine supports interaction terms, making this a rigorous, formally inferable heterogeneity test.",
  "expected_learning": "If the interaction coefficient confidence interval excludes zero on the negative side, it indicates a more negative commute‑sleep association among women; if it excludes zero on the positive side, it indicates a more negative association among men; if the interval includes zero, the result is inconclusive and leaves the question of a sex difference open.",
